  "system": {
    "description": "The nomad biomorph is optimized for operating in desert environments. They incorporate many transgenic traits from camels: thicker eyelashes to keep out sand, a third eyelid to dislodge grit, a complex of arteries and veins for better brain cooling, elongated noses to trap exhaled water vapor, and sometimes hooves. They carry a distributed network of fat tissue that can be relocated around their body to adapt to high or low temperatures.",
